{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/451309-concerning-the-alpha-and-omega-of-history","id":451309,"title":"Concerning the Alpha and Omega of History","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-20T22:30:47-07:00","id":451309,"title":"Concerning the Alpha and Omega of History","content":"I have read every plot ultimately pivots on the question of fraud or force and the characters action/inaction to resolve the effect. For example, miscommunication can be considered accidental fraud. Fraud also includes the camo of the tiger in the deep grass. The dog that buries its bone to keep it from others. Force the dog that unburies the bone of another, combined with fraud because it is done while they are not looking. Governments exist to regulate and prohibit these forces. Government decides just how much we are allowed to be fools to fraud and responsible in our own defense. What other crimes indicate there is another natural force besides these two (fraud and force)? What is that natural power which governments exist to regulate and prohibit our action in? I ask because it seems this would be thematic in all of the games we play here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T10:18:14-07:00","id":454546,"title":"","content":"I think all I can contribute is a Killer Croc level response - &quot;I threw a rock at him.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T10:24:27-07:00","id":454554,"title":"","content":"Or I could post something about how I believe this is a false dichotomy to begin with as there are many more reasons and methods for motivating humanity than forcing them or fooling them, unless you would consider EVERY attempt at appealing to humanity's better nature and continued preservation and existence as &quot;fooling them&quot;.<br /> <br /> If that's the case, not only is that a horribly pessimistic attitude, but it discounts the motivations of anyone who's truly attempted an altruistic method of motivation upon his fellow man. It seems totally nihilistic in it's approach in that it makes the continued existence of humanity rather worthless if all they do for their own good and the good of others is only thru force or fraud.<br /> <br /> I realize the title attempts to make a scale by referencing the beginning and the ending on a biblical scale, but the basic text and crux of the statements contained within make it clearly an attempt to disprove a &quot;one or the other&quot; line of thought which is, most likely, already decided upon by the original poster and nothing we state here will change that formed opinion.<br /> <br /> <br /> tl:dr - <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Papa Bear - graduate of the Henry McCoy school of debate","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T11:10:18-07:00","id":454613,"title":"","content":"Assuming I correctly understand the OP...<br /> <br /> By your definitions, the Government employs both fraud and force to control the population. Its &quot;power&quot; comes from a monopoly on resources that can be deployed for forceful or fraudulent purposes.<br /> <br /> The cynicism that extends from this line of thinking can only lead to nihilism, so I'm going to say that the correct answer to your question is &quot;<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mu_%28negative%29#The_text_of_the_Mu-koan\" target=\"_blank\">Mu</a>.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T16:28:02-07:00","id":455008,"title":"","content":"&quot;Fraud and force&quot; presents far too simple a view of human methods and motivations.<br /> <br /> At risk of immodesty, I suggest Googling my essay, &quot;Designing Cultures the Shomshak Way&quot; for a wider view of power, with a gaming focus. I also suggest the work of psychologist Jonathan Haidt on motivations, particularly his book The Righteous Mind on political psychology.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T19:00:08-07:00","id":464136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/451309-concerning-the-alpha-and-omega-of-history?p=454546#post454546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think all I can contribute is a Killer Croc level response - &quot;I threw a rock at him.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The summation of this story acts on a plot centered on an act of force.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/451309-concerning-the-alpha-and-omega-of-history?p=454554#post454554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I believe this is a false dichotomy</div> </div> </div> </div>Belief isn't evidence of an additional natural force.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> many more reasons and methods for motivating humanity </div> </div> </div>This isn't a question of motivation. Although governments and religions attempt to outlaw our thoughts, we have yet to reach a point where this is practical. Motive is irrelevant. A hate crime is merely and only a crime of force or fraud about which a motive is presumed. The criminal, regardless of motive, effected some action that resulted in the crime. That action is either applied force to achieve a physical effect or fraud in order to evade notice of some condition or expected result.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> who's truly attempted an altruistic ... motivation </div> </div> </div>What force or deception prevented this attempt?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;one or the other&quot; line of thought which is, most likely, already decided upon by the original poster and nothing we state here will change that formed opinion. </div> </div> </div>This has nothing to do with debate. The statement that all plots derive from a question of &quot;Frode o Forza&quot; is a reference from analysis of classical literature. I am not framing this for debate. I am asking what real adversarial actions about which plots form are not derived from either an application of physical effect or an application of deception.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/451309-concerning-the-alpha-and-omega-of-history?p=454613#post454613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Government employs both fraud and force to control the population.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all. The government employs laws to regulate or punish those who would use Fraud and Force.<br /> <br /> I was asking what else. If centuries of analysis are correct and all our literary themes and legal prohibitions center around crimes of fraud and force - then there are only two enemies of justice: misapplied power and misapplied deception. The misapplication comes from motive, but the action the motive causes apparently is either fraud or force. Love is not an action, it is a motive resulting in actions of fraud or force. The same is true of hate, greed, selfishness, lust, or even honor, compassion, mercy, etc.<br /> <br /> The plot of a story comes about when there is conflict. The example above - A rock was thrown by one person at another (not to the other). So, if Fraud and Force are not the limit of what plots are centered upon, what else is there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}